---
// Earth's lite route — where a visitor goes who cannot, or will not, run the Earth globe.
//
// IT IS THE GALLERY, WHICH ALREADY EXISTED AT `/`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF THIS PAGE. Mars's lite
// route is a page written for the purpose because Mars has no heroes to show; Earth's content was
// the site's front page before there was a second body to need a route name. This file gives that
// content the name every body's lite route has, so `liteRoute` is `/<slug>/lite/` on both planets
// and a third body copies a row instead of inheriting a coincidence.
//
// WHY IT IS NOT A REDIRECT. The route is a redirect TARGET — the pre-paint guard `location.replace`s
// here before the page paints — so a hop through it would be a second navigation on exactly the
// devices least able to afford one, and a static build has no 301 to offer, only a meta refresh.
//
// The canonical link points the other way ON PURPOSE. The gallery's identity is the site's front
// page: that is what is linked, shared and indexed, and this URL exists for the routing symmetry
// rather than to compete for it. Root-relative because `astro.config.ts` sets no `site` — an
// absolute URL here would be a second spelling of the origin with nothing checking it.
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Gallery from "../../components/Gallery.astro";
import { pageTitle } from "../../lib/pageTitle";
---

<Base title={pageTitle("Gallery")} body="earth" pageRole="lite" spotlight={true} quality={true}>
  <link slot="head" rel="canonical" href="/" />
  <Gallery />
</Base>
